  - drought
  - heat
  - National Family Health Survey
  - India
  - climate and health
abstract: >-
  Code and aggregate results of a pre-specified analysis linking children under five in
  NFHS-4 (2015–16) and NFHS-5 (2019–21) to trimester-specific and early-life rainfall deficit
  (SPI-3 dryness) and maximum-temperature anomaly at their survey cluster and to ENSO conditions in
  pregnancy, with birth weight, height-for-age, stunting, diarrhoea and anaemia as outcomes
  (survey-weighted fixed-effects models). The NFHS microdata and GPS data are available from the
  DHS Program on registration and are not redistributed; the repository contains no record-level
  or cluster-level data.
